questions.prompt:
An API reflects origins for which the Python suffix check below succeeds, and sends Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true. Assume the attacker controls the candidate origin and eligible victim credentials are sent. Which untrusted domain passes?

```python
def allowed(origin):
    return origin.endswith(
        "example.com")
```

questions.workedExample:
Go character by character:

```
<   -> &lt;
b   -> b
>   -> &gt;
Tom -> Tom
&   -> &amp;
...
```

Result: `&lt;b&gt;Tom &amp; Jerry&lt;/b&gt;`. The browser renders it as the visible text `<b>Tom & Jerry</b>`, not bold. That's the whole point: data stays data.

